f common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le15ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past Tense and Past Continuous tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are   finished.</br> You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I played baseball all through grade school. How about you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I wasn't interested in sports much. I was always playing around on the computer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.</br> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"italic\">-ied</span>.</br> Irregular verbs change in different ways.</br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by  the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask \u2026 ?</span></br> <span class=\"italic\"> Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For Past Continuous, we add <span class=\"italic\"> was/were + verb -ing</span> to verbs.  Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add <span class=\"italic\"> -ing</span>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"grow\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"grew\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were growing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rented\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were renting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"play\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"played\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were playing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"told\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were telling\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"try\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tried\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were trying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"saw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"----------\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"attack\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"attacked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were attacking\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to grow up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to grow from a child into an adult"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter and Sally both grew up in Boston. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about your personal past and history."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grade school"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a term used more in the US to refer to the years of elementary school from 1st grade to 8th grade"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter played baseball all through grade school."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "revolution"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a war in which one group fights to break free from another"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The American Revolution started because the people wanted to have their own country."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "colonists"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "people that were sent by their country to live in an another area far away controlled by their home country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The colonists didn't want to be ruled by another country and wanted to be called Americans."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "settle"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to set up a new life in a new land or country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The colonists were sent from England to come settle in America."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "worth it"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the result or reward is good for the effort or money you put in"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's ride up the hill. The view from the top is worth it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research or ask other people about war monuments in your region."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Select one monument. Take notes in English on what battle the monument honors."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 5 sentences about the history of this monument. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask your partner in English what they know about this monument. Tell them the information you learned. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research history in my region."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I take notes in English on specific information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write complete statements on a historical monument."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I exchange knowledge with my partner about local history. "}]}]}